27, "baseline_margin": -9.79, "analyst_adjustment": -0.71, "key_factors": ["R+9 district with Republican incumbent Addison McDowell renominated", "McDowell's dominant fundraising edge; Jefferson held under $15,000 cash", "Unanimous Solid/Safe R expert ratings; markets price Jefferson near 8%", "No public polling; a Democratic-leaning national environment is the main counterweight"], "rationale": "The district's nine-point Republican lean, McDowell's incumbency and roughly six-to-one fundraising advantage, and a unanimous set of Solid or Safe Republican ratings from nine raters outweigh the Democratic-favorable national environment. Jefferson is a credible nominee as High Point's mayor but lacks the money to change the race's structure.", "watch": "Late national Democratic investment or polling showing Jefferson competitive in the Greensboro and High Point media market would be the clearest sign the race is narrowing.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Addison McDowell (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's sixth district leans firmly Republican, and incumbent Addison McDowell is seeking re-election after winning renomination. The seat was redrawn in 2024 and sits about nine points to the right of the country, giving Democrats a steep hill in the Piedmont Triad region. Democratic nominee Cyril Jefferson, the mayor of High Point, emerged from a competitive primary and brings local name recognition, but his campaign has raised roughly $200,000 and had under $15,000 in the bank in the latest filings.\n\nMcDowell has raised more than $1.2 million and holds a large cash advantage, and every major race rater places the district in the Solid or Safe Republican column, with a few calling it Likely Republican. Prediction markets give Jefferson roughly an eight percent chance. A favorable national climate for Democrats is the main variable, but the structural advantages point to a Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -10.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0423, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0544, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0437, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -10.5}]}